% Problem 25. Chace vol. II pl. 48 (photograph XII, register 2), PDF pp. 143-144; Peet pp. 61-62 (Pl. H).
No. 25
"{A quantity, '2 of it added to it,} becomes it: 16."
  1      2
  '2     1
% no total written (2 and its half make 3); 3 is then reckoned with to find 16, with no sentence
\ 1      3
  2      6
\ 4      12
  2/3    2
\ '3     1
% no total written; the ticked multipliers give 5 '3, which is then multiplied by 2
  1      5 '3
\ 2      10 2/3
"The doing as it occurs."
10 2/3        % "{The quantity}" (the words in red in Chace)
5 '3          % "'2" (its half)
Total 16.
